/* Why phyphox asks for access to the microphone (audio experiments such as the acoustic stopwatch or the audio spectrum). Shown by iOS in its permission prompt, the first time phyphox needs this access; the user then allows or denies it. "Export function" means exporting data from an experiment's actions menu. */
"NSMicrophoneUsageDescription" = "phyphox records audio from the microphone like from other sensors and analyzes it according to the selected experiment. The data will only be exported from the app if the user elects to do so using the export function.";
/* Why phyphox asks for access to devices on the local network. Shown by iOS in its permission prompt, the first time phyphox needs this access; the user then allows or denies it. "Remote access" is the feature that shows a running experiment in a web browser on another device; use the same term as in the app. */
"NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription" = "phyphox accesses your local network when an experiment configuration is loaded from a device on your network, when an experiment reads from or sends data to local devices (for example Wi-Fi measurement hardware or an MQTT broker), and when remote access is enabled to control an experiment from a web browser.";
/* Why phyphox asks for access to the location (GPS experiments, for example measuring speed or altitude). Shown by iOS in its permission prompt, the first time phyphox needs this access; the user then allows or denies it. "Export function" means exporting data from an experiment's actions menu. */
"NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription" ="phyphox records location data from GPS like from other sensors and analyzes it according to the selected experiment. The data will only be exported from the app if the user elects to do so using the export function.";
/* Why phyphox asks for permission to add images to the photo library. Shown by iOS in its permission prompt, the first time phyphox needs this access; the user then allows or denies it. "Share screenshot" quotes the entry in an experiment's actions menu; use the same words as your translation of that entry (share). */
"NSPhotoLibraryAddUsageDescription" = "phyphox can add screenshots to your photo library if you select \"Share screenshot\" from the experiment menu.";
/* Why phyphox asks for access to motion data (the "Motion & Fitness" permission of iOS, which covers for example the barometer). Shown by iOS in its permission prompt, the first time phyphox needs this access; the user then allows or denies it. */
"NSMotionUsageDescription" = "phyphox reads your phone's sensors to allow using them in physics experiments.";
/* Why phyphox asks for access to the camera: scanning QR codes of experiments, and camera and depth sensor (LiDAR/ToF) experiments. Shown by iOS in its permission prompt, the first time phyphox needs this access; the user then allows or denies it. Keep the abbreviations LiDAR and ToF. */
"NSCameraUsageDescription" = "phyphox uses the camera to scan QR codes, which can be used to add custom experiment configurations. The camera is also used as a measurement tool for optical experiments and experiments using the depth sensor (LiDAR/ToF).";
/* Why phyphox asks for access to Bluetooth (external sensors and devices, for example microcontroller projects). Shown by iOS in its permission prompt, the first time phyphox needs this access; the user then allows or denies it. Only read by iOS versions older than 13, which phyphox no longer supports; the text is the same as NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription. Keep the web address. */
"NSBluetoothPeripheralUsageDescription" = "phyphox has the ability to read from external Bluetooth sensors and write data to external Bluetooth devices. You can learn more about this feature and supported devices on http://phyphox.org/ble.";
/* Why phyphox asks for access to Bluetooth (external sensors and devices, for example microcontroller projects). Shown by iOS in its permission prompt, the first time phyphox needs this access; the user then allows or denies it. Keep the web address. */
"NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription" = "phyphox has the ability to read from external Bluetooth sensors and write data to external Bluetooth devices. You can learn more about this feature and supported devices on http://phyphox.org/ble.";

